# Remote hosts allowed to receive folders from this repository.
#
# One entry per line:
#
#   <host> <folder> [folder...]
#
# Blank lines and text after '#' are ignored. The host is validated against
# [A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]* and must also be a configured SSH alias or DNS
# name. Folders are top-level directories of this repository; anything with a
# slash, a leading dot or '..' is rejected before a command runs.
#
# A folder only leaves this machine when the selected host is listed here and
# the folder is named on that host's line. Adding a folder to a host is the
# only way to let the script send it.
#
# Destination layout on the remote (relative to the remote login home):
#
#   apps     -> ~/apps/<host>/   only apps/<host>/ from this repo
#   scripts  -> ~/scripts/       the whole scripts/ tree
#
# Accounts are deliberately split: apps stacks live in the unprivileged 'app'
# account, scripts go to the 'admin' account only.
#
# Raspberry Pi over Tailscale, see ~/.ssh/config.
app.duck    apps
admin.duck  scripts
